(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[10 1 "// The module _thread (PY6f; Modules/_threadmodule.c): threads over goroutines under the GIL (thread_gil.go,"] [11 1 "// PYS10 (a)), locks and re-entrant locks whose waits release the GIL (on the main thread interruptible by a"] [12 1 "// signal's handler), thread handles (start_joinable_thread, join, _shutdown joining the non-daemon threads at"] [13 1 "// the end), thread identity, and _local, thread-local data: one dict per thread, swapped in at each access."] [22 1 "// pyLock is a lock: a token in ch when it is free (acquire receives it, release sends it back)."] [35 1 "// acquire takes the lock: at once when it is free; else, blocking, within timeout (negative: no limit)."] [57 1 "// pyRLock is a re-entrant lock: its owner's ident (0: none), the count, the lock under it."] [66 1 "// threadHandle is a thread's handle (ThreadHandle): its ident, its state, done closed when it ends."] [69 14 "// handleNotStarted, handleRunning, handleDone"] [72 15 "// by start_joinable_thread (joinable)"] [94 1 "// timeoutMax is TIMEOUT_MAX in seconds (PY_TIMEOUT_MAX / 1e6 on Linux)."] [97 1 "// lockAcquireArgs reads acquire(blocking=True, timeout=-1): blocking and the timeout (negative: none)."] [134 1 "// timeoutArg is a join's or a get's timeout: None or absent no limit (negative), else seconds."] [155 1 "// currentIdent is the running thread's ident."] [158 1 "// allThreads are the started threads that run, oldest first, with their idents (queue 220: faulthandler's dumps read"] [159 1 "// them from goroutines that do not hold the GIL, so under a lock of their own and not from threadInfos)."] [166 1 "// threadsNewestFirst are the threads as CPython's interpreter lists them: the newest first, the main thread last."] [180 1 "// threadIdentOf is t's ident as the registry holds it (the main thread's mainThreadIdent)."] [190 1 "// mainInterpThread is the main thread of the running interpreter (set by NewInterp)."] [215 1 "// shutdownHandles are the non-daemon threads' handles, joined by _shutdown."] [218 1 "// startThread runs fn(args) in a new thread under the GIL (thread_run): SystemExit ends it silently, another"] [219 1 "// exception goes to sys.unraisablehook."] [254 1 "// threadOSNames are the OS threads' names (pthread_setname_np's), by ident: one OS thread's in every interpreter (queue 230)."] [257 1 "// threadsAllowed is do_start_new_thread's checks of the interpreter's config (queue 230)."] [266 2 "// do_start_new_thread at shutdown (queue 253): _PyInterpreterState_GetFinalizing"] [273 1 "// writeUnraisable is PyErr_FormatUnraisable: sys.unraisablehook called with the exception, the message and the"] [274 1 "// object, or, when it is the default hook, CPython's text on stderr."] [280 2 "// format_unraisable_v: an exception with no traceback gets the current frame's (PyTraceBack_Here)"] [286 3 "// write_unraisable_exc: no sys.stderr (None, or sys's dictionary cleared at shutdown) writes nothing"] [319 1 "// WaitForThreadShutdown is Py_FinalizeEx's wait_for_thread_shutdown: threading._shutdown() when threading was"] [320 1 "// imported, its error printed."] [339 1 "// localState is a _local's per-thread dicts and its constructor's arguments (localobject)."] [348 1 "// localDict makes o's dict the running thread's, made (and __init__ called again, as CPython's"] [349 1 "// _ldict) on the thread's first access."] [566 3 "// gh-123940 (queue 253): at shutdown the other threads cannot run, so join() raises rather than hang"] [662 3 "// get_native_id (queue 535): the main thread's is the process's id, as Linux's main thread's tid is its pid (a"] [663 3 "// spawned or forkserver child's main thread is not its parent's: test_process_mainthread_native_id); another"] [664 3 "// thread's its ident, unique in the process"] [819 4 "// PyErr_SetInterruptEx: only a Python handler is tripped; on the main thread it runs at once (CPython's"] [820 4 "// next eval breaker check is at the call's return)"] [827 3 "// set_name and _get_name: the thread's name as pthread_setname_np keeps it on Linux, encoded in utf-8,"] [828 3 "// cut at a NUL and at _NAME_MAXLEN (15) bytes, read back by os.fsdecode's rule"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[105 34] [171 35] [171 43] [174 26] [184 35] [235 34] [236 29] [281 25] [285 32] [287 37] [304 101] [305 37] [306 48] [333 32] [360 21] [372 56] [373 70] [509 40] [528 50] [666 27] [710 38] [741 34] [794 34] [798 36] [821 26] [853 43]]} (go/file "builtins_thread.go" :imports [


